The function takes rows and returns only the PUBLIC_COLUMNS from each, so the docstring can say that accurately. [tool_use propose_change {"path":"register/export.py","summary":"Add docstring to export_comments describing its input, output, and that only public columns are kept.","diff":"--- a/register/export.py\n+++ b/register/export.py\n@@ -3,6 +3,15 @@\n PUBLIC_COLUMNS = ['reference', 'address', 'comment_date', 'stance', 'comment_text']\n \n def export_comments(rows):\n+    \"\"\"Return the public columns of each comment row for export.\n+\n+    Args:\n+        rows: An iterable of mappings, each containing at least the\n+            PUBLIC_COLUMNS keys.\n+\n+    Returns:\n+        A list of dicts, one per input row, containing only the keys in\n+        PUBLIC_COLUMNS. Private fields such as objector details and\n+        internal notes are excluded.\n+    \"\"\"\n     out = []\n     for row in rows:\n         out.append({c: row[c] for c in PUBLIC_COLUMNS})\n"}]
